### Step 2: Generate a feature for the maximum consecutive rank difference
This feature helps capture whether the ranks in the hand form a sequence (useful for straights or straight flushes).

python
# max_consecutive_rank_diff
# Feature description: The largest difference between consecutive ranks when the ranks are sorted.
# Usefulness: For straights or straight flushes, this value should be 1 consistently across all consecutive pairs of ranks. Any gap >1 indicates the hand is not sequential.
df['max_consecutive_rank_diff'] = df[['V2', 'V4', 'V6', 'V8', 'V10']].apply(
    lambda row: max(sorted(row) - sorted(row[:-1])), axis=1
)
end

